---
source: crates/standalone/fixture/src/lib.rs
---
Send the folder to its site and start a deploy.

Usage: ink push [OPTIONS]

Options
      --no-wait          Return when the build is queued, without waiting for it
      --wait <SECONDS>   Seconds to wait for the build before stopping; it keeps
                         going on the server [default: 300]
      --poll <MS>        Milliseconds between two looks at the build
                         [default: 1000]
      --batch <BYTES>    Most bytes of files in one request; the server's own
                         limit applies when it is smaller
      --batch-files <N>  Most files in one request; the server's own limit
                         applies when it is smaller [default: 1000]
      --rounds <N>       How many times the tree is sent and the files it lacks
                         answered, before giving up [default: 3]

Account
      --api <URL>          The API's address, `http://host[:port]`;
                           `account.api` in the config file [env: INK_API]
      --site <ID>          The site's id; `account.site` in the config file
                           [env: INK_SITE]
      --org <ID>           Act as this organization, by its id: the site is one
                           of its sites, and the key's role there is what is
                           checked. See `ink org list` [env: INK_ORG]
      --timeout <SECONDS>  Seconds one call may take [default: 30]
                           [env: INK_TIMEOUT]
      --retries <N>        How many more times a call that is safe to repeat is
                           tried when the network fails [default: 2]
                           [env: INK_RETRIES]
      --retry-wait <MS>    Milliseconds before the first retry; each wait is
                           twice the one before [default: 500]
                           [env: INK_RETRY_WAIT]

Global  -C, --json, -q, -v, --color, --no-progress, --log, --log-file
        (see `ink --help`)
More    ink push --help adds examples, notes and exit codes
